  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The area of a circle is doubled when its radius \\(r\\) is increased by \\(n.\\) Then \\(r\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(n(\\sqrt2+1)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(n(\\sqrt2-1)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(n\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(n(2-\\sqrt2)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{n\\pi}{\\sqrt2+1}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The doubled-area condition is \\[ \\pi(r+n)^2=2\\pi r^2. \\] Since the radii are positive, \\(r+n=\\sqrt2\\,r.\\) Thus \\[ r=\\frac{n}{\\sqrt2-1} =n(\\sqrt2+1). \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Translate the doubled-area condition into \\(\\pi(r+n)^2=2\\pi r^2\\)",
        "After taking positive square roots, solve \\(r+n=\\sqrt2\\,r\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
